* (-) 42.3. [feature] Notes {* 42.3}

  Rich-text note creation, search, and sharing — progressing from
  wireframe prototype through functional implementation to pixel-perfect
  polish across all platforms.

  Stages:
  ~ Stage 1 — /Wireframe/: basic CRUD with placeholder UI, proves the data model
  ~ Stage 2 — /Functional/: full feature set with working UI, no visual polish
  ~ Stage 3 — /Polished/: pixel-perfect UI, animations, accessibility, performance
  ~ Stage 4 — /Advanced/: collaboration, version history, templates

  Pre-requisites:
  - (x) {* 42.1} Authentication — user identity
  - (x) {* 42.6.3} Database — notes tables
  - (-) {* 42.8.1} API Client SDK — typed API calls from FE/Mobile
  - (x) {* 42.8.2} UI Component Library — design system tokens


** (x) 42.3.1. Stage 1 — Wireframe {* 42.3.1}

   Minimal viable slice: plain-text notes with CRUD operations and
   placeholder UI. Goal is to validate the data model, API contract,
   and end-to-end data flow before investing in rich features or polish.

*** (x) 42.3.1.1. Design {* 42.3.1.1}
    User story:
    - /As a developer, I want a working notes CRUD with basic UI on all
      platforms, so that we can validate the data model and API contract
      before building rich features./

    Artifacts:
    - Database schema: `notes` table (id, owner_id, title, body, timestamps)
    - Low-fidelity wireframes for list and editor screens
    - API contract: OpenAPI spec for notes endpoints

*** (x) 42.3.1.2. Implementation {* 42.3.1.2}

**** (x) 42.3.1.2.1. Backend {* 42.3.1.2.1}
     - (x) Notes CRUD API (create, read, update, delete)
       - AC: returns 201/200/204; validates title length ≤200 chars
       - AC: soft-delete with 30-day retention before permanent removal
     - (x) List endpoint with basic pagination
       - AC: offset-based pagination (limit + offset params)
       - AC: default sort by updated_at descending
     - (x) Owner-scoped access (users see only their own notes)
       - AC: 404 on access to another user's note (no information leak)

**** (x) 42.3.1.2.2. Frontend {* 42.3.1.2.2}
     - (x) Notes list — plain table with title, date, action buttons
       - AC: renders all notes; no search or filtering yet
       - AC: click row opens editor; delete button with confirm dialog
     - (x) Note editor — single textarea with title input
       - AC: plain text only; save button; no autosave
       - AC: unsaved changes warning on navigation (browser beforeunload)
     - (x) Placeholder layout matching wireframe grid
       - AC: sidebar + content area; no responsive breakpoints yet

**** (x) 42.3.1.2.3. Mobile {* 42.3.1.2.3}
     - (x) Notes list screen with flat list
       - AC: renders title + date; tap opens editor
       - AC: uses default React Native components (no custom styling)
     - (x) Note editor screen with text input
       - AC: title + body fields; keyboard avoidance
       - AC: save button in navigation header
     - (x) Navigation wiring (list → editor → back)
       - AC: stack navigation; back gesture works on iOS

*** (x) 42.3.1.3. Verification {* 42.3.1.3}
    - Backend: 3 test suites (CRUD operations, pagination, access scoping)
    - Frontend: 2 test suites (list rendering, editor save/navigate)
    - Mobile: 2 test suites (list rendering, editor save)
    - Integration: E2E create → read → update → delete flow

*** (x) 42.3.1.4. Validation {* 42.3.1.4}
    - (x) Wireframe review with product team — data model approved
    - (x) REST acceptance scripts for notes API
    - (x) Basic smoke test on all platforms


** (x) 42.3.2. Stage 2 — Functional {* 42.3.2}

   Full feature set: rich-text editing, search, sharing, offline support.
   UI is functional and usable but uses default component styling — no
   visual polish, animations, or pixel-perfect alignment.

*** (x) 42.3.2.1. Design {* 42.3.2.1}
    User stories:
    - /As a user, I want to format notes with headings, lists, and code
      blocks, so that my notes are structured and readable./
    - /As a user, I want to search my notes by keyword and share them
      with other users, so that I can find and collaborate on content./

    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.3.1} Stage 1 — Wireframe (data model validated)
    - (-) {* 42.4} Notifications — share notifications (BE/FE ready, Mobile pending)
    - (x) {* 42.8.4} Migration System — schema changes for search index + sharing

*** (x) 42.3.2.2. Implementation {* 42.3.2.2}

**** (x) 42.3.2.2.1. Backend {* 42.3.2.2.1}
     - (x) Full-text search with database indexing
       - AC: results within 200ms for up to 10k notes
       - AC: supports phrase matching and field-scoped queries (title, body)
     - (x) Note sharing with permission model (view / edit)
       - AC: shared users receive notification via {* 42.4}
       - AC: permissions revocable; owner can transfer ownership
     - (x) Markdown rendering and HTML sanitisation
       - AC: strips script tags and event handlers; preserves formatting
       - AC: rendering happens server-side for consistency across platforms
     - (x) Upgrade pagination to cursor-based
       - AC: replaces offset-based; no drift on concurrent inserts
       - AC: sort by created, updated, or title
     - (x) Note pinning and archiving
       - AC: pinned notes appear first in list regardless of sort
       - AC: archived notes excluded from default list; accessible via filter

**** (x) 42.3.2.2.2. Frontend {* 42.3.2.2.2}
     - (x) Markdown editor with live preview
       - AC: split-pane or toggle mode; syntax highlighting in source
       - AC: toolbar for headings, bold, italic, lists, code, links
     - (x) Search bar with debounced query and filter controls
       - AC: 300ms debounce; filters: owned, shared, archived, pinned
     - (x) Share dialog with user search and permission selector
       - AC: autocomplete user search; permission dropdown (view/edit)
     - (x) Keyboard shortcuts for common actions
       - AC: Ctrl+S save, Ctrl+N new note, Ctrl+/ toggle preview
     - (x) Autosave with conflict detection
       - AC: saves 3s after last keystroke; conflict banner if server
             version diverges; offers merge or overwrite
     - (x) Pin and archive actions on note list items
       - AC: icon buttons on hover; visual indicator for pinned notes

**** (x) 42.3.2.2.3. Mobile {* 42.3.2.2.3}
     - (x) Rich-text toolbar above keyboard
       - AC: floating toolbar with bold, italic, heading, list, code
       - AC: toolbar scrolls horizontally if items exceed screen width
     - (x) Offline note creation with sync queue
       - AC: notes created offline stored in local SQLite
       - AC: sync on reconnect; last-write-wins with manual override
     - (x) Pull-to-refresh on notes list
       - AC: loading indicator; list updates without scroll position reset
     - (x) Share via native share sheet
       - AC: generates share link; deep link opens note in app
     - (x) Swipe actions (pin, archive, delete)
       - AC: swipe-right to pin/unpin; swipe-left for archive/delete
       - AC: undo toast visible for 5s

*** (x) 42.3.2.3. Verification {* 42.3.2.3}
    - Backend: 6 test suites (search, sharing, permissions, pagination,
      rendering, pin/archive)
    - Frontend: 6 test suites (editor, search, share dialog, shortcuts,
      autosave, conflict handling)
    - Mobile: 5 test suites (rich toolbar, offline sync, share, swipe,
      pull-to-refresh)
    - Integration: E2E note lifecycle including search, share, offline sync

*** (x) 42.3.2.4. Validation {* 42.3.2.4}
    - (x) 6 QA test scenarios (create, search, share, offline, conflict,
