    - (x) REST acceptance scripts for all notes endpoints
    - (x) Cross-platform sync verification (web ↔ mobile)


** (-) 42.3.3. Stage 3 — Polished {* 42.3.3}

   Pixel-perfect UI aligned to design system, micro-interactions,
   transitions, accessibility audit, and performance optimisation. No new
   features — only refinement of everything built in Stage 2.

   /Scope driven by: QA feedback from Stage 2 validation, revised design
   specs from design team, and accessibility audit findings./

*** (x) 42.3.3.1. Design {* 42.3.3.1}
    User stories:
    - /As a user, I want the notes experience to feel fast, smooth, and
      visually polished, so that the app feels professional and pleasant
      to use daily./
    - /As a user with accessibility needs, I want notes to be fully
      navigable with keyboard and screen reader, so that I can use the
      app without barriers./

    Artifacts:
    - High-fidelity mockups from design team (Figma)
    - Animation spec: transitions, loading skeletons, micro-interactions
    - Accessibility audit checklist (WCAG 2.1 AA)

*** (-) 42.3.3.2. Implementation {* 42.3.3.2}

**** (x) 42.3.3.2.1. Backend {* 42.3.3.2.1}
     - (x) Response time optimisation on list and search endpoints
       - AC: P95 <150ms for list (100 notes); P95 <200ms for search
       - AC: database query plans reviewed; indices verified
     - (x) Thumbnail generation for note preview cards
       - AC: first 3 lines of body rendered as plain-text preview
       - AC: preview cached; invalidated on note update
     - (x) ETags for conditional requests (cache validation)
       - AC: 304 Not Modified on unchanged content; reduces payload

**** (-) 42.3.3.2.2. Frontend {* 42.3.3.2.2}
     - (x) Design system token alignment (colours, spacing, typography)
       - AC: all hardcoded values replaced with {* 42.8.2} tokens
       - AC: dark mode support via token layer (no manual overrides)
     - (x) Loading skeletons for list and editor
       - AC: skeleton matches final layout dimensions; no layout shift
       - AC: shown for >200ms to avoid flash
     - (x) Transition animations (page enter/exit, list reorder)
       - AC: 200ms ease-out for page transitions
       - AC: list items animate on reorder (pin/unpin), add, remove
     - (-) Responsive breakpoints (desktop, tablet, mobile web)
       - AC: 3-column on desktop (sidebar + list + editor)
       - AC: 2-column on tablet (list + editor)
       - AC: single-column on mobile web (stack with back navigation)
     - ( ) Accessibility audit and remediation
       - AC: all interactive elements keyboard-navigable (tab order)
       - AC: ARIA labels on icon-only buttons; live regions for toasts
       - AC: colour contrast ratio ≥4.5:1 on all text
       - AC: screen reader announces note content structure (headings)
     - ( ) Performance: bundle size and render optimisation
       - AC: editor lazy-loaded (not in initial bundle)
       - AC: list virtualised for >100 notes (no DOM bloat)
       - AC: Lighthouse performance score ≥90

**** (-) 42.3.3.2.3. Mobile {* 42.3.3.2.3}
     - (x) Design system alignment (native components match Figma specs)
       - AC: font sizes, colours, spacing match design tokens
       - AC: platform-specific adjustments (iOS vs Android) documented
     - (x) Haptic feedback on key interactions
       - AC: light tap on save; subtle pulse on pin/unpin
       - AC: error haptic on validation failure
     - (-) Smooth transitions and gesture animations
       - AC: swipe-to-archive uses spring physics animation
       - AC: editor open/close: shared element transition on note title
       - AC: keyboard appearance doesn't cause layout jump
     - ( ) Accessibility: VoiceOver (iOS) and TalkBack (Android)
       - AC: all screens navigable with screen reader
       - AC: custom actions announced (swipe actions, toolbar buttons)
       - AC: dynamic type / font scaling support (up to 200%)
     - ( ) Performance: startup time and scroll performance
       - AC: notes list renders first frame <500ms from navigation
       - AC: scroll at 60fps with 500+ notes (FlatList optimisation)
       - AC: memory usage stable during extended editing sessions

