** ( ) 42.3.4. Stage 4 — Advanced {* 42.3.4}

   Collaborative editing, version history, and note templates. Builds on
   the polished foundation from Stage 3.

*** ( ) 42.3.4.1. Design {* 42.3.4.1}
    User stories:
    - /As a team member, I want to edit a note simultaneously with
      colleagues and see their cursors in real time, so that we can
      collaborate without version conflicts./
    - /As a user, I want to view the history of changes to a note and
      restore a previous version, so that I can recover from accidental
      edits or deletions./
    - /As a user, I want to create notes from templates (meeting notes,
      project brief, checklist), so that I can start with a useful
      structure instead of a blank page./

    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.3.3} Stage 3 — Polished (stable, accessible UI)

*** ( ) 42.3.4.2. Implementation {* 42.3.4.2}

**** ( ) 42.3.4.2.1. Backend {* 42.3.4.2.1}
     - ( ) Operational transform (OT) or CRDT engine for concurrent editing
       - AC: concurrent edits from 2+ users merge without data loss
       - AC: cursor positions broadcast to all participants via WebSocket
     - ( ) Version history with diff generation
       - AC: stores snapshots on save (debounced, max 1 per minute)
       - AC: diff endpoint returns inline additions/deletions between versions
       - AC: restore endpoint creates new version from historical snapshot
     - ( ) Template CRUD API
       - AC: system templates (read-only) + user-created templates
       - AC: "create from template" duplicates content into new note
     - ( ) Concurrent editor presence (who is viewing/editing)
       - AC: presence shown as avatar pills at top of note
       - AC: stale presence (no heartbeat for 60s) auto-removed

**** ( ) 42.3.4.2.2. Frontend {* 42.3.4.2.2}
     - ( ) Collaborative cursors and selections in editor
       - AC: each collaborator shown with coloured cursor and name label
       - AC: selections highlighted in collaborator's colour
     - ( ) Version history sidebar with timeline
       - AC: scrollable list of versions with author, date, summary
       - AC: click version shows diff; restore button with confirmation
     - ( ) Template picker on note creation
       - AC: grid of template cards with preview; search by name
       - AC: "blank note" always first option
     - ( ) Presence indicator bar (active editors)
       - AC: avatar stack at top of editor; tooltip shows full names

**** ( ) 42.3.4.2.3. Mobile {* 42.3.4.2.3}
     - ( ) Real-time collaborative editing (shared cursor display)
       - AC: cursors shown as coloured carets; smooth position updates
     - ( ) Version history screen with restore action
       - AC: list view; tap to preview version; long-press to restore
     - ( ) Template selection bottom sheet on new note
       - AC: scrollable grid; tap to create from template
     - ( ) Active editors indicator in navigation bar
       - AC: avatar circles; tap shows full participant list

*** ( ) 42.3.4.3. Verification {* 42.3.4.3}
    - ( ) Backend: OT/CRDT convergence tests, version history, templates,
          presence lifecycle
    - ( ) Frontend: collaborative cursor rendering, diff display, template
          picker, presence indicator
    - ( ) Mobile: collaborative editing, version restore, template sheet
    - ( ) Integration: 3-user concurrent editing across web and mobile

*** ( ) 42.3.4.4. Validation {* 42.3.4.4}
    - ( ) QA scenarios: concurrent editing conflict resolution, version
          restore, template creation and use
    - ( ) Performance: collaborative editing latency <100ms between users
    - ( ) Stress test: 10 concurrent editors on single note
